    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2773" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτιο-λογέω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>inquire into causes, reason, account for</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὲρ τῶν μετεώρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epicur.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					1p.31U.
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Diocl.Fr.
				112
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				6.7.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.689b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ζητούμενον</span> Aenesid.
			ap. <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>P.</u>
				1.181
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.Lac.
				1012.68
			</span></i>:— 
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τοῦ συνδέσμου
				ᾐτιολογημένον ἐστίν</span> the conjunction indicates
			that <i>the cause resides in . .</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Conj.</u>
				235.9
			</span></i>.</div>
